id: pm-1rfy0y
title: Advertise safe linked-test command replacement after an immutable-command edit refusal
description: "During evidence maintenance, test --update-index --set-json with a command field correctly refused rewriting immutable command/provenance identity, but returned generic Command failed guidance without an executable replacement route. The successful current route is an exact command removal followed by adding the replacement with fresh provenance. Preserve the completed metadata-editing and deterministic replacement implementations and improve this distinct refusal UX."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[3]: agent-ux,linked-tests,recovery
created_at: "2026-10-26T00:21:26.298Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-01T23:05:43.797Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-01T21:06:46.090Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-01T21:06:46.090Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: Refusal exposes a stable code and selector-aware supported replacement recovery; SDK CLI and MCP agree on immutable command/provenance semantics; Executed recovery replaces only the selected command and preserves unrelated tests plus append-only history; Metadata-only edits remain supported and preserve provenance
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: low
confidence: 90
resolution: linked_test_command_immutable carries a scope-preserving remove plus add-json retry built from the selected entry; other unsupported keys refuse with linked_test_patch_fields_unsupported and the editable domain.
expected_result: A command edit is refused without a write and the advertised retry replaces only the selected entry with fresh provenance.
actual_result: "Executing the CLI retry replaced only the selected entry in one tests_add event, the other entry is unchanged and history verifies."
dependencies[3]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
